-- Raid spawns Legends of Azeroth Pandaria 5.4.8 has and SkyFire lacks (GPL v2, world DB of 2024-07-22).
-- Creatures: skyfire_port_plan/tools/SpawnFill.pl. For each entry LoA spawns more often on a map, same-entry spawns are
-- paired one to one by distance and the unpaired LoA spawns are added, unless any SkyFire creature stands within
-- 4 yards; waypoint paths (id guid*10) and per-spawn addons come along. Gameobjects: the same rules (gofill.py).
-- Left out: LoA spawns in a pool or game event, and entries the SkyFire scripts of that map summon themselves
-- (static copies would double them): Hyjal's attack waves (Ghoul, Abomination, Shadowy Necromancer, Ancient Wisp,
-- Archimonde Channel Target, Horde Healing Ward), Buru's hatchlings and Ossirian's crystal (AQ20), Magtheridon's
-- Burning Abyssals, the Parasitic Shadowfiends (BT), Anveena (Sunwell), the Karazhan event bosses, the ToC
-- encounter controllers and Anub'arak, Alexstrasza's Gift / Heart of Magic (Eye of Eternity), Sapphiron Birth,
-- Razorscale's broken harpoons, an extra Gift of the Observer no script handles, and King Varian / Cairne in AQ20.
-- Computed against world_dev with the open raid PRs applied (#207 Ulduar, #209 ICC, #211 Karazhan, #213 Naxxramas).
-- GUID block 9691000+ (creatures 9691000-9691894, gameobjects 9691000-9691255). No database names; safe to run twice.

-- Onyxia's Lair (249): creatures
DELETE FROM `creature` WHERE `guid` BETWEEN 9691000 AND 9691011;

DELETE FROM `creature_addon` WHERE `guid` BETWEEN 9691000 AND 9691011;

